From: OpenWrt E8450 investigation <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: add NETSYSv1 QDMA fc_th control

Expose the global NETSYSv1 QDMA flow-control/RED threshold register
(fc_th, 0x1a10) for measurement: read it back in qdma_regs and allow a
diagnostic write via a new qdma_fc debugfs file. The driver init value
is FC_THRES_DROP_MODE | FC_THRES_DROP_EN | FC_THRES_MIN (0x00174444).

This register was investigated as a possible hardware tail-drop lever
that would bound QDMA queue latency. It is inert on MT7622: the vendor
writes the same init value in every driver revision and never tunes it,
and lowering it produced no observable change in queue behaviour. The
readback is retained because that negative result is worth being able
to re-verify cheaply; see docs/README.md's closed hardware dead ends.

This patch previously also added a per-queue "MIB" counter readout
(QTX_MIB_IF debug mode at 0x1abc, plus the 64-bit byte-counter pair at
QTX_CFG+0x8/+0xc added later by qos-11). That was removed: the MIB
debug mode does not exist on NETSYSv1. MediaTek gates the entire block
to NETSYSv2-or-greater in every vendor generation (mtk-openwrt-feeds
25.12 999-eth-90 proprietary-debugfs patch:
"if (mtk_is_netsys_v2_or_greater(eth))"; the 5.4 equivalent uses
"if (!MTK_HAS_CAPS(eth->soc->caps, MTK_QDMA_V1_1))", which MT7622 also
fails), and assigns qtx_mib_if = 0x46bc only for mt7986_reg_map and
mt7988_reg_map - never for the NETSYSv1 register map, which has no such
field at all. Reading 0x1abc on this SoC returned zero on ~95% of
samples and small implausible values otherwise, including during
transfers where that queue's own leaky bucket was provably the
bottleneck.

There is no per-queue counter on this hardware. The offload path's real
accounting is the PPE per-flow counters (mt7622_data sets
.has_accounting = true), which mtk_ppe's own stats path already uses.

All controls are NETSYSv1-gated, serialized under qdma_sch_lock, and
change nothing unless written. NETSYSv2/v3 and MT7621 are untouched.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt E8450 investigation <noreply@example.invalid>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -992,6 +992,8 @@
 
 	seq_printf(s, "tx_sch_rate_value=0x%08x\n",
 		   mtk_r32(eth, map->qdma.tx_sch_rate));
+	seq_printf(s, "fc_th_value=0x%08x\n",
+		   mtk_r32(eth, map->qdma.fc_th));
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -1198,6 +1200,45 @@
 	.write	= mtk_qdma_txq_write,
 };
 
+/* qos-05: write the global QDMA flow-control/RED threshold register
+ * (fc_th, 0x1a10). Diagnostic only: the driver init value is
+ * FC_THRES_DROP_MODE | FC_THRES_DROP_EN | FC_THRES_MIN (0x4444); lowering
+ * the threshold was investigated as a hardware tail-drop lever and found
+ * inert on this SoC.
+ */
+static ssize_t mtk_qdma_fc_write(struct file *file, const char __user *ubuf,
+				 size_t count, loff_t *ppos)
+{
+	struct mtk_eth *eth = file->private_data;
+	const struct mtk_reg_map *map = eth->soc->reg_map;
+	unsigned long long parsed;
+	char buf[16], extra;
+
+	if (!mtk_qdma_v1_override_supported(eth))
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+	if (*ppos || count >= sizeof(buf))
+		return -EINVAL;
+	if (copy_from_user(buf, ubuf, count))
+		return -EFAULT;
+	buf[count] = '\0';
+
+	if (sscanf(buf, "%llx %c", &parsed, &extra) != 1 ||
+	    parsed > 0xffffffffULL)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	spin_lock_bh(&eth->qdma_sch_lock);
+	mtk_w32(eth, (u32)parsed, map->qdma.fc_th);
+	spin_unlock_bh(&eth->qdma_sch_lock);
+
+	return count;
+}
+
+static const struct file_operations mtk_qdma_fc_fops = {
+	.owner	= THIS_MODULE,
+	.open	= simple_open,
+	.write	= mtk_qdma_fc_write,
+};
+
 static void mtk_qdma_debugfs_init(struct mtk_eth *eth)
 {
 	struct dentry *root;
@@ -1219,7 +1260,9 @@
 	     IS_ERR_OR_NULL(debugfs_create_file("qdma_sch", 0200, root, eth,
 						&mtk_qdma_sch_fops)) ||
 	     IS_ERR_OR_NULL(debugfs_create_file("qdma_txq", 0200, root, eth,
-						&mtk_qdma_txq_fops))))
+						&mtk_qdma_txq_fops)) ||
+	     IS_ERR_OR_NULL(debugfs_create_file("qdma_fc", 0200, root, eth,
+						&mtk_qdma_fc_fops))))
 		goto error;
 
 	return;
